Use Arg request, response
response~content_type = "text/plain"
-- CGI-contract probe for the variable x topology matrix. Each active line
-- below emits one reconstructed CGI variable as "name=[value]". The matrix
-- framework (RunHTTPTests.rex + the CGI-contract tests in RexxHTTP.testGroup)
-- deploys this same probe across the twelve topologies and asserts each
-- value against the contract literal for that (variable, topology) cell.
--
-- To bring a NEW variable under contract: uncomment its line here, run the
-- matrix once to SEE what it emits in each of the twelve cells, decide with
-- the CGI contract in hand which values are correct, and paste those twelve
-- literals as a new row in the contract table. Never predict the value in
-- code -- the probe reports, the table records, so the test never
-- reimplements what it checks.
Say "request_url=["request~request_url"]"
Say "script_name=["request~script_name"]"
-- Not yet under contract (validate before activating):
Say "path_info=["request~path_info"]"
Say "path_translated=["request~path_translated"]"
Say "filename=["request~filename"]"
Say "script_filename=["request~script_filename"]"
Say "request_uri=["request~request_uri"]"
Say "uri=["request~uri"]"
Say "document_uri=["request~document_uri"]"
-- Say "requested_file=["request~requested_file"]"
Say "query_string=["request~query_string"]"
